@startuml
title PEP-28: Model Context Protocol (MCP) Server Architecture & Request Flow

actor "AI Agent / Client\n(Claude, Cursor, Script)" as Client
participant "AWS WAF &\nAPI Gateway" as APIGW
participant "EDI MCP Server\n(FastAPI / FastMCP)" as MCP
database "Amazon ElastiCache\n(Redis Cache)" as Cache
participant "EDI Gatekeeper\n(Reverse Proxy)" as Gatekeeper
participant "EDI IAM" as IAM
participant "PASTA+ Core Services\n(Data Package & Audit Mgr)" as PASTA
database "AWS S3\n(Data Entities - PEP-11)" as S3

autonumber

== Authenticated Request & Bot Mitigation ==
Client -> APIGW: MCP Request (JSON-RPC 2.0 via SSE/HTTP)\nHeader: X-API-Key: <EDI-API-Key>\nUser-Agent: EDI-MCP-Agent/1.0
note over APIGW
  1. AWS WAF evaluates IP reputation & bot signatures
  2. API Gateway validates Usage Plan & applies rate limits
     (Token bucket per Tier: Free, Pro, Enterprise)
end note
APIGW -> MCP: Forward authorized request

== Cache Evaluation ==
alt Read Request (Search / Metadata / Report)
  MCP -> Cache: Check cache (hash key of endpoint + params)
  alt Cache Hit
    Cache --> MCP: Return cached XML / JSON payload
    MCP --> APIGW: Fast response (0 backend load)
    APIGW --> Client: MCP Tool/Resource response
  end
end

== Backend Dispatch & IAM Authentication ==
MCP -> Gatekeeper: REST Request + API Key\nHeader: User-Agent: EDI-MCP-Agent/1.0\nHeader: EDI-Agent-Client-ID: <id>
Gatekeeper -> IAM: Validate API Key (PEP-15 / PEP-27)
IAM --> Gatekeeper: EDI Auth Token (authenticated/human level)
Gatekeeper -> PASTA: Authorized REST call with EDI Token

== Response Handling & Raw Streaming ==
alt Small Payload (Search results, XML metadata, JSON)
  PASTA --> Gatekeeper: REST XML / JSON response
  Gatekeeper --> MCP: REST response
  MCP -> Cache: Cache response (TTL: 1h - 24h)
  MCP --> APIGW: Format as MCP Tool / Resource
  APIGW --> Client: Tool response (JSON-RPC)
else Large Data Entity (readDataEntity)
  PASTA --> Gatekeeper: Stream data stream / chunked transfer
  Gatekeeper --> MCP: Pipe raw byte stream (no memory buffering)
  MCP --> APIGW: Stream raw bytes through MCP response
  APIGW --> Client: Stream payload (client LLM handles budgeting/truncation)
end

@enduml
